src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:6:/// A collection to keep track of which deposit outpoints have already been
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:7:/// relayed, in order to ensure that we don't credit the same deposit more than
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:8:/// once.
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:9:///
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:10:/// Outpoints are stored in a set, and added to a queue with an expiration
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:11:/// timestamp so we can prune the set.
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:12:///
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:13:/// It is important for safety that outpoints can not expire from the set until
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:14:/// after they are no longer considered valid to relay, otherwise there is risk
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:15:/// of the network crediting a deposit twice. Care should be taken to configure
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:16:/// usage of this collection to set timestamps properly to ensure this does not
src/bitcoin/outpoint_set.rs:17:/// happen.
