src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:38:///
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:39:/// Signatory sets will be constructed by iterating over the validator set in
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:40:/// descending order of voting power, skipping any validators which have not
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:41:/// submitted a signatory xpub.
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:42:///
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:43:/// This constant should be chosen to balance the tradeoff between the
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:44:/// decentralization of the signatory set and the size of the resulting script
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:45:/// (affecting fees).
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:46:///
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:47:/// It is expected that future versions of this protocol will use aggregated
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:48:/// signatures, allowing for more signatories to be included without making an
src/bitcoin/signatory.rs:49:/// impact on script size and fees.
