src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:348:/// A queue of Bitcoin block headers, along with the total estimated amount of
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:349:/// work (measured in hashes) done in the headers included in the queue.
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:350:///
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:351:/// The header queue is used to validate headers as they are received from the
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:352:/// Bitcoin network, ensuring each header is associated with a valid
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:353:/// proof-of-work and that the chain of headers is valid.
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:354:///
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:355:/// The queue is able to reorg if a new chain of headers is received that
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:356:/// contains more work than the current chain, however it can not process reorgs
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:357:/// that are deeper than the length of the queue (the length will be at the
src/bitcoin/header_queue.rs:358:/// configured pruning level based on the `max_length` config parameter).
