src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:290:/// BTCDelegationStatus is the status of a delegation. The state transition path
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:291:/// is PENDING -> ACTIVE -> UNBONDED with two possibilities:
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:292:/// 1. the typical path when timelock of staking transaction expires.
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:293:/// 2. the path when staker requests early undelegation through MsgBTCUndelegate
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:294:///    message.
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:298:    /// PENDING defines a delegation that is waiting for covenant signatures to
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:299:    /// become active.
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:301:    /// ACTIVE defines a delegation that has voting power
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:303:    /// UNBONDED defines a delegation no longer has voting power:
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:304:    /// - either reaching the end of staking transaction timelock
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:305:    /// - or receiving unbonding tx with signatures from staker and covenant
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:306:    ///   committee
src/babylon/proto/mod.rs:308:    /// ANY is any of the above status
