src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:2:/// Consider we have a Merkle tree with following structure:
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:3:///             ROOT
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:4:///            /    \
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:5:///       H1234      H5555
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:6:///      /     \       \
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:7:///    H12     H34      H55
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:8:///   /  \    /  \     /
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:9:/// H1  H2  H3  H4  H5
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:10:/// L1  L2  L3  L4  L5
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:11:/// To prove L3 was part of ROOT we need:
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:12:/// - btc_transaction_index = 2 which in binary is 010
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:13:/// (where 0 means going left, 1 means going right in the tree)
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:14:/// - merkle_nodes we'd have H4 || H12 || H5555
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:15:/// By looking at 010 we would know that H4 is a right sibling,
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:16:/// H12 is left, H5555 is right again.
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:20:    /// Valid bitcoin transaction containing OP_RETURN opcode.
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:23:    /// Index of transaction within the block. Index is needed to determine if
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:24:    /// currently hashed node is left or right.
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:27:    /// List of concatenated intermediate merkle tree nodes, without root node
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:28:    /// and leaf node against which we calculate the proof. Each node has 32
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:29:    /// byte length. Example proof can look like: 32_bytes_of_node1 ||
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:30:    /// 32_bytes_of_node2 ||  32_bytes_of_node3 so the length of the proof will
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:31:    /// always be divisible by 32.
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:34:    /// Valid btc header which confirms btc_transaction.
src/babylon/proto/btccheckpoint.rs:35:    /// Should have exactly 80 bytes
