src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:443:/// The default fee rate to be used to pay miner fees, in satoshis per virtual
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:444:/// byte.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:447:/// `Checkpoint` is the main structure which coordinates the network's
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:448:/// management of funds on the Bitcoin blockchain.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:449:///
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:450:/// The network periodically creates checkpoints, which are Bitcoin transactions
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:451:/// that move the funds held in reserve. There is a singular sequential chain of
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:452:/// checkpoints, and each checkpoint has an associated signatory set. The
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:453:/// signatory set is a list of public keys of the signers performing the
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:454:/// decentralized custody of the funds held in reserve.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:455:///
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:456:/// Checkpoints are each associated with a main transaction, the "checkpoint
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:457:/// transaction", which spends the reserve output of the previous checkpoint
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:458:/// transaction and the outputs of any incoming deposits. It pays out to the the
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:459:/// latest signatory set (in the "reserve output") and to destinations of any
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:460:/// requested withdrawals. This transaction is included in the third batch of
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:461:/// the `batches` deque.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:462:///
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:463:/// Checkpoints are also associated with a set of transactions which pay out to
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:464:/// the recipients of the emergency disbursal (e.g. recovery wallets of nBTC
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:465:/// holders), if the checkpoint transaction is not spent after a given amount of
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:466:/// time (e.g. two weeks). These transactions are broken up into a single
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:467:/// "intermediate emergency disbursal transaction" (in the second batch of the
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:468:/// `batches` deque), and one or more "final emergency disbursal transactions"
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:469:/// (in the first batch of the `batches` deque).
