src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1081:/// `CheckpointQueue` is the main collection for the checkpointing process,
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1082:/// containing a sequential chain of checkpoints.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1083:///
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1084:/// Once the network has processed its first deposit, the checkpoint queue will
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1085:/// always contain at least one checkpoint, in the `Building` state, at the
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1086:/// highest index in the queue.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1087:///
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1088:/// The queue will only contain at most one checkpoint in the `Signing` state,
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1089:/// at the second-highest index in the queue if it exists. When this checkpoint
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1090:/// is stil being signed, progress will block and no new checkpoints will be
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1091:/// created since the checkpoints are in a sequential chain.
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1092:///
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1093:/// The queue may contain any number of checkpoints in the `Complete` state,
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1094:/// which are the checkpoints which have been fully signed and are ready to be
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1095:/// broadcast to the Bitcoin network. The queue also maintains a counter
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1096:/// (`confirmed_index`) to track which of these completed checkpoints have been
src/bitcoin/checkpoint.rs:1097:/// confirmed in a Bitcoin block.
